   "verbSense": "do; the general verb, and sports and games are things you 'do'",
   "englishVerb": "play",
   "trap": "English 'play' pulls toward asobu. For gaming in general, friends say geemu suru or yaru (geemu yatteru). With a specific title, gamers also say kono geemu asonda?, and geemu de asobu (play around with a game) is fine.",
