   "noun": "piano",
   "particle": "o",
   "verb": "narau",
   "verbJa": "習う",
   "verbSense": "learn from a teacher, take lessons in",
   "englishVerb": "learn",
   "trap": "English 'learn' leads to benkyou suru, but piano o benkyou shita sounds like studying it as a subject. Lessons with a teacher are narau: piano naratteta. oboeru is memorising or picking something up yourself (shigoto oboeta = I've learned the job).",
